# The repo fleet, every 12 hours, to /Volumes/local -- a portable USB disk.
# Copy to ~/.config/system/mirror-sync/mirrors-repos.conf ($SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG/mirror-sync) and set your own paths.
# The nightly list is mirrors.conf; this one runs on its own schedule because
# ~/repos is too large for a nightly pass that also writes to iCloud.
#
# Format matches mirrors.conf, plus the optional third field: comma-separated
# rsync exclude patterns for that pair alone.
#
# The destination is under "Backup Local", which mirrors.conf does NOT copy to
# iCloud -- unlike /Volumes/local/Backup.
#
# Run this list ADDITIVE (MIRROR_SYNC_ADDITIVE=1, no --delete), with
# overwrites preserved under MIRROR_SYNC_BACKUP_ROOT. An exact mirror would
# propagate a `git reset --hard` into the only other copy and then report
# success, and uncommitted work lost that way exists nowhere else. So this
# mirrors working trees, not just remotes.
#
# The excludes are regenerable trees only. `dist/` and `build/` are
# deliberately NOT excluded: both names are also used for hand-written files,
# and excluding a directory that can hold uncommitted work would lose it.
/Users/example/repos|/Volumes/local/Backup Local/repos|node_modules/,.venv/,venv/,target/,__pycache__/,*.pyc,.mypy_cache/,.pytest_cache/,.ruff_cache/,.next/,.turbo/,.gradle/,.tox/,*.egg-info/
